// Use : Setting of component (material)
// Goal : To simulate cone calorimeter
// Material : Douglas Fir (sensitivity_douglas_fir.jl nominal values)
// Unit : Heat capacity (J/kgK), Heat of reaction (J/kg)
//
// Notes:
//   - Virgin DF cp is piecewise linear via instantaneous transition reactions:
//     DF (T<=323K): cp = -18.0 + 4.134*T  [HFM low-T segment]
//     DF_M (323-425K): cp = -33.6 + 4.182*T  [interpolated segment]
//     DF_H (T>425K): cp = -2139.3 + 9.137*T  [STA high-T segment]
//   - Intermediate cp's are cumulative-yield blends of high-T virgin and char cp.
//   - Heat of sorption integrated from 6% to 0% MC (dry basis):
//     HoS(MC) = (2450.42 + 875.64*exp(-0.1122*MC)) kJ/kg
//     avg = (1/6)*integral_0^6 HoS dMC = 3088 kJ/kg.
//   - Gas transport = lambda_gas * sqrt(M_ref/M_i), lambda_gas=3e-5, M_ref=0.029.
//   - TK sign convention: HEAT > 0 exothermic, HEAT < 0 endothermic
//     (opposite of Julia/standard thermodynamic convention).

COMPONENT:	MOISTURE
STATE:		L
DENSITY:	1e6  0  0  0
HEAT CAPACITY:	5.2e3  -6.7  1.1e-2  2
CONDUCTIVITY:	0.145  0  0  0
TRANSPORT:	2e-5  0  0  0
EMISSIVITY & ABSORPTION:  0.81  1000

COMPONENT:	WATER_VAPOR
STATE:		G
DENSITY:	1e5  0  0  0
HEAT CAPACITY:	1716.7  0.4154  1.530e-4  2
CONDUCTIVITY:	0.025  0  0  0
TRANSPORT:	3.808e-5  0  0  0
EMISSIVITY & ABSORPTION:  0.81  1000

COMPONENT:	DF
STATE:		S
DENSITY:	530.0  0  0  0
HEAT CAPACITY:	-18.0  4.134  0  0
CONDUCTIVITY:	0.145  0  0  0
TRANSPORT:	5e-7  0  0  0
EMISSIVITY & ABSORPTION:  0.81  1000

COMPONENT:	DF_M
